    dcterms:source <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf>;
    rdfs:comment "Care parameter describing the temperature used in a washing process."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process>;
    txt-connector:modellingNote "Expected SI quantity kind for a Celsius temperature value: quantities:TEMC; expected unit: units:degreeCelsius."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceLocator "JRC Preparatory Study, Section 9.2.2.2, printed page 125, lines 3296-3327; JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.7.2, printed pages 394-395, lines 10227-10248."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceType txt-connector:adaptedDefinition;
    rdfs:subClassOf txt-process:CareParameter.
txt-process:WeavePatternSpecification a owl:Class;
    rdfs:label "Weave pattern specification"@en;
    dcterms:source <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf>;
    rdfs:comment "A process target specification stating the weave pattern to be produced."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process>;
    txt-connector:modellingNote "The process-side target remains distinct from the resulting characteristic represented in Textile Structure."@en, "The JRC identifies weave pattern as one of the weaving parameters affecting fabric characteristics. The relation is represented as weak influence annotations rather than as deterministic OWL axioms."@en, "Weave pattern is a fabric construction parameter that may affect visual appearance, permeability, drape and handle. The relation is represented as weak influence because the direction depends on the specific weave and yarns."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceLocator "JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.2, printed pages 493-495, lines 11902-11920; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 182, printed page 302; caption line 9114."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceType txt-connector:adaptedDefinition;
    txt-connector:typicalInfluenceOn txt-structure:FabricDrape, txt-structure:FabricBreathability, txt-structure:FabricAppearance, txt-structure:FabricHandle;
    rdfs:subClassOf txt-process:FabricConstructionParameter.
txt-structure:FabricAppearance a owl:Class;
    rdfs:label "Fabric appearance"@en;
    dcterms:source <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf>;
    skos:altLabel "Fabric visual appearance"@en;
    txt-connector:evidenceStatus txt-connector:explicitEvidence, txt-connector:stronglyImpliedEvidence;
    rdfs:comment "Fabric visual characteristic concerning the overall visible appearance or visual quality of a fabric."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure>;
    txt-connector:modellingNote "Fabric appearance is represented as a fabric visual characteristic in TEXTILE_STRUCTURE. Observed changes in fabric appearance after use or cleaning cycles should be represented in TEXTILE_DURABILITY or TEXTILE_ASSESSMENT, not as the structural characteristic itself."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceLocator "JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.2, printed pages 488-491, lines 11875-11888; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 178, printed page 302; caption line 9109."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceType txt-connector:adaptedDefinition;
    rdfs:subClassOf txt-structure:FabricVisualCharacteristic.
txt-structure:FabricHandle a owl:Class;
    rdfs:label "Fabric handle"@en;
    dcterms:source <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf>;
    skos:altLabel "Fabric hand"@en, "Fabric softness"@en, "Hand feel"@en;
    txt-connector:evidenceStatus txt-connector:explicitEvidence;
    rdfs:comment "Fabric tactile characteristic concerning softness, smoothness, flexibility and overall sensation when touched."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure>;
    txt-connector:modellingNote "Fabric handle is modelled as a fabric tactile characteristic, not as a simple fabric structural characteristic and not as an assessment result. Quantitative or qualitative measurements of softness, handle or touch should be represented through the assessment module when a concrete method or result is recorded."@en, "Table 180 relates fabric softness or handle to fibre characteristics. The influence links are represented as weak annotation-level relations, not as deterministic OWL causal axioms."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceLocator "JRC Preparatory Study, Section 13.10.2, printed pages 488-491, lines 11875-11888; JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, Table 178, printed page 302; caption line 9109."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceType txt-connector:adaptedDefinition;
    rdfs:subClassOf txt-structure:FabricTactileCharacteristic.
txt-process:WeavingProcess a owl:Class;
    rdfs:label "Weaving process"@en;
    dcterms:source <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf>;
    txt-connector:evidenceStatus txt-connector:explicitEvidence;
    rdfs:comment "Fabric manufacturing process in which two sets of yarns are interlaced at right angles on a loom."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process>;
    txt-connector:modellingNote "Weaving is generally used for relatively more rigid and stronger fabrics, depending on yarns, weave pattern and product application."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceLocator "JRC Section 3.3.1, Table 8, printed pages 27-29; table caption at line 546."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceType txt-connector:adaptedDefinition;
    txt-connector:typicalInfluenceOn txt-durability:FabricStrength, txt-structure:FabricRigidity;
    rdfs:subClassOf txt-process:FabricManufacturingProcess.
txt-structure:FabricRigidity a owl:Class;
    rdfs:label "Fabric rigidity"@en;
    dcterms:source <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf>;
    txt-connector:evidenceStatus txt-connector:reconstructedEvidence, txt-connector:stronglyImpliedEvidence;
    rdfs:comment "Fabric structural characteristic denoting rigidity or stiffness."@en;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure>;
    txt-connector:modellingNote "Fabric rigidity may influence wrinkling and deformation behaviour, but the direction and acceptability depend on product type and fabric construction."@en, "Reconstructed concept added to support relations between fabric manufacturing methods and fabric behaviour."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceLocator "JRC Annex 13.10.2, Tables 178-179, printed pages 488-490; captions at lines 11875 and 11877."@en;
    txt-connector:sourceType txt-connector:modellingAbstraction;
    txt-connector:typicalInfluenceOn txt-durability:Wrinkling;
    rdfs:subClassOf txt-structure:FabricStructuralCharacteristic.
